{"parentUuid":"51ed5949-0389-49eb-8160-afcbbc242bee","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_012JrujZrFjWtZ57JPniouyG","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"additionalContext\":\"<context_guidance>\\n  <tip>\\n    When you intend to PROCESS the output (filter, count, parse, aggregate), use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute(commands, queries) for multiple commands or mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language: \\\"javascript\\\", code: \\\"...\\\") for one — the raw output stays in the sandbox and only what you print enters your conversation. Shell stays the right surface when you intend to OBSERVE a short fixed output or when you are mutating state (git, mkdir, rm, mv, navigation); if you use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language: \\\"shell\\\"), write syntax for the host shell.\\n  </tip>\\n</context_guidance>\"}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/pretooluse.mjs\"","durationMs":96},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5f95acce-ca10-4bf5-b9be-a79fdb23fda4","timestamp":"2026-09-22T22:47:43.048Z","session_id":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","version":"2.1.280","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"5f95acce-ca10-4bf5-b9be-a79fdb23fda4","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_additional_context","content":["<context_guidance>\n  <tip>\n    When you intend to PROCESS the output (filter, count, parse, aggregate), use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute(commands, queries) for multiple commands or mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language: \"javascript\", code: \"...\") for one — the raw output stays in the sandbox and only what you print enters your conversation. Shell stays the right surface when you intend to OBSERVE a short fixed output or when you are mutating state (git, mkdir, rm, mv, navigation); if you use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language: \"shell\"), write syntax for the host shell.\n  </tip>\n</context_guidance>"],"hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_012JrujZrFjWtZ57JPniouyG","hookEvent":"PreToolUse"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e018ceaa-0402-4557-af55-ff127023a36e","timestamp":"2026-09-22T22:47:43.049Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nPreToolUse:Bash hook additional context: <context_guidance>\n  <tip>\n    When you intend to PROCESS the output (filter, count, parse, aggregate), use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute(commands, queries) for multiple commands or mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language: \"javascript\", code: \"...\") for one — the raw output stays in the sandbox and only what you print enters your conversation. Shell stays the right surface when you intend to OBSERVE a short fixed output or when you are mutating state (git, mkdir, rm, mv, navigation); if you use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language: \"shell\"), write syntax for the host shell.\n  </tip>\n</context_guidance>\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887