{"parentUuid":"c78245fc-f9bc-4416-a2b4-b45c6126d162","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"87d6c547-b2ad-4d4f-b4f7-18e6b02e26a7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y3T9ZqWcHjwCpaDXfaKiXP","type":"tool_result","content":"OK .\n## main...origin/main\nOK DataBase_GPS_Reporting\n## main...origin/main\nOK PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA\n## main...origin/main\nOK TOS_Evidence_Brief\n## main...origin/main\nOK TypeSafe_Sandbox\n## main...origin/main\nOK Football/PFF_Data_Project\n## main...origin/main\nOK Football/SpringPlayerEvals_SymAnalysis\n## master...origin/master\nMISSING AI_Analyst\nMISSING Linda_Projects","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5f9413fc-e6e0-4136-a0df-fca47f29fa87","timestamp":"2026-09-22T22:49:56.628Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"OK .\n## main...origin/main\nOK DataBase_GPS_Reporting\n## main...origin/main\nOK PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA\n## main...origin/main\nOK TOS_Evidence_Brief\n## main...origin/main\nOK TypeSafe_Sandbox\n## main...origin/main\nOK Football/PFF_Data_Project\n## main...origin/main\nOK Football/SpringPlayerEvals_SymAnalysis\n## master...origin/master\nMISSING AI_Analyst\nMISSING Linda_Projects","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/PLATFORM.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":18,"oldLines":7,"newStart":18,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | Folder | What it is |"," |---|---|"," | `CLI_Dev/` | CLI development scratch. Built CLIs land in `~/go/bin/`. Holds `printing-press/` — the Printing Press workspace (`library/`, `manuscripts/`), moved here from `~/printing-press` on 2026-09-07. Now covered by the backup manifest — but `CLI_Dev` routes to **`ssd` only**, so it is protected only on nights CRASHBOX is attached, not by GitHub or Drive. `~/printing-press` is now a symlink to it; tools that assume the old path still work. |","-| `Life-OS/` | OneDrive ↔ Google Drive sync scripts and two `com.eric.*` launchd plists. Moved from `~/Desktop/Life-OS` on 2026-09-07; script and plist paths repointed, manifest entry added (`personal`/`ssd` — reclassify if wrong). **Plists are on disk but NOT loaded** — nothing is scheduled. Overlaps the KeystoneOS `dailybackup` Drive rsync; decide which one survives. |","+| `Life-OS/` | OneDrive ↔ Google Drive sync scripts and two `com.eric.*` launchd plists (on disk, not loaded). Overlaps the KeystoneOS `dailybackup` Drive rsync. State and the open keep-or-retire decision: `Life-OS/docs/STATUS.md`. |"," | `AgentAssist/` | Agent assistance experiments → own `CLAUDE.md` |"," | `_ARCHIVE/AI_Analyst/` | **Archived 2026-09-09.** Course clone, never used. GitHub repo set read-only. |"," | `Terminal_Fluency/` | CLI-learning mission. Lessons + quiz. Learns through real repairs, not exercises. |"]},{"oldStart":26,"oldLines":7,"newStart":26,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | `Bucket/` | Catch-all + `docs/TOOLING-OPTIMIZATION.md` |"," | `PythonScripts_2024/` | Reference shelf of standalone 2024 Python scripts (scraping, team/player data, early dashboards, one-off analyses), flattened into `scripts/`. Nothing live — lift anything worth reusing into a real repo. Own `AGENTS.md` + `CLAUDE.md`. Git repo, created 2026-09-14 on Windows. |"," | `KnowledgeManagement/` | Personal file and knowledge management system: three-tier setup, file naming convention, Fireflies-to-Obsidian meeting import. Own `CLAUDE.md`. **Disk is the source of truth**; the Claude cloud project is only a pointer. |","-| `TypeSafe_Sandbox/` | Sandbox for the TypeSafe System One API (the Jev model: typed judgments and probabilities, not generated text). Holds `setup_global_key.sh` and `smoke_test.py`. **The API key is not in the repo, and nothing about it syncs between machines** — Windows reads `~/.claude/typesafe.env` (auto-ignored by the dotclaude whitelist), macOS uses the Keychain (service `typesafe-api-key`) exported by `~/.zshenv`, per the `machine.macos.md` rule. The key starts with `apikey_`; dropping that prefix returns 401. Both machines have a key as of 2026-09-19 — Windows verified end to end against the live API, Mac added but not verified from the Windows side. Claude Code carries the matching skill as plugin `typesafe@typesafe-ai`. Created 2026-09-19. |","+| `TypeSafe_Sandbox/` | Sandbox for the TypeSafe System One API (the Jev model: typed judgments and probabilities, not generated text). Holds `setup_global_key.sh` and `smoke_test.py`. **The API key is not in the repo, and nothing about it syncs between machines** — Windows reads `~/.claude/typesafe.env` (auto-ignored by the dotclaude whitelist), macOS uses the Keychain (service `typesafe-api-key`) exported by `~/.zshenv`, per the `machine.macos.md` rule. The key starts with `apikey_`; dropping that prefix returns 401. Claude Code carries the matching skill as plugin `typesafe@typesafe-ai`. Per-machine key status: `TypeSafe_Sandbox/docs/STATUS.md`. |"," "," ## Generated artifacts (not source)"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/RESEARCH.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":12,"oldLines":6,"newStart":12,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | `LibraryProject/` | Book library → advisor entries → own `CLAUDE.md` |"," | `Weekly_Research_Review/` | \"Research in 5\": weekly one-paper review. Deck PDF for Teams, post, email, running index. Outputs on `_DRIVE/07_EDUCATION/Research_in_5` → own `AGENTS.md` |"," | `Epilepsy-Baseball-Research/` | Epilepsy + baseball literature review |","+| `TOS_Evidence_Brief/` | Thoracic outlet syndrome in overhead throwing athletes. One-page briefing note + 14-page evidence review, built to Word/PDF by `scripts/` → own `AGENTS.md` |"," | `BookInbox/` | Staging for books not yet ingested |"," | `reMarkale_extract/` | reMarkable highlight extraction. Note the spelling — \"reMarkale\". |"," | `ContextVault/` | Context storage experiment |"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/docs/STATUS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":12,"newStart":1,"newLines":20,"lines":[" # STATUS — ~/DEV workspace root"," "," ## Current state","+- 2026-09-22 (Windows, doctor-plus): context audit against the 6 context-engineering shifts. The memory-compiler SessionStart injection was 20,037 chars because the Windows checkout was 6 commits behind origin; a fast-forward took it to 3,772. PRs: DEV #7 (router state out), claude-skills #4 (skill-creator canonical, CreateSkill retired, closeout Cowork note), dotclaude #3 (CreateSkill off), TypeSafe_Sandbox #26, Life-OS #1. Open: Eric adds the CLAUDE.md skills-are-tools line (auto mode blocked it), deletes CreateSkill/, and re-uploads 3 skills to claude.ai.","+- 2026-09-22 (Windows): Closed out the 09-21 handoffs. All leftover worktrees cleared from `_INBOX`,","+  `DataBase_GPS_Reporting` and `DEV` — one of them (`status+closeout-0917`) held an unmerged 09-17","+  handoff, recovered and merged as `bb266b9`. `TOS_Evidence_Brief` scaffolded (PR #1) and added to","+  `RESEARCH.md` (PR #5). Google Drive's 162 sync errors traced to Windows junctions: SpeedProfiling's","+  renv library moved out of DEV via `RENV_PATHS_LIBRARY_ROOT`, leaving 2 expected errors. Detail:","+  `docs/handoffs/2026-09-22-worktree-cleanup-renv-drive-tos-scaffold.md`."," - 2026-09-21: Repaired Claude Code prompt blocking on the Mac. The synced","   `UserPromptSubmit` rule pointed to a missing skill-router file. Removed only that","   rule, then completed the Mac-specific setup. The live list and roster now match at","   149 skills. All accuracy, fail-open, degraded-config, and time-limit checks passed.","   The hook is enabled and the other hooks remain. Detail is in","   `TypeSafe_Sandbox/docs/STATUS.md`.","+- 2026-09-17 (Windows): **`DexaProject` removed from `~/DEV` on this machine too.** The Mac moved it to Google Drive on 09-09 and the router already said it was gone, but the Windows copy was still in the DEV root — the router was false on this machine. Deleted after verifying the Drive copy strictly supersedes it (Drive HEAD `5ab14b6` is a descendant of local `962ce2d`, `.mdb` byte-identical, CSVs differing only in line endings). Both router files now carry each machine's path to the one Drive folder; merged as PR #2 (`cb6c3f2`). Detail: `docs/handoffs/2026-09-17-dexaproject-windows-removal.md`. **DEV now discovers 143 repos, not 144.**"," - 2026-09-14 Windows closeout: all 144 discovered DEV repos are clean against their recorded upstreams. Migration items 2-4 and 6 are complete; detailed handoff: `docs/handoffs/2026-09-14-windows-migration-closeout.md`."," - 2026-09-14 (Mac): `/doctor-plus` context audit. 40 owned skills set `name-only` in `~/.claude/settings.json`; step/analysis logs moved out of Risk_Stratification_Engine and Ath_Medicine guidance files; FaceComps and PlayCalls `CLAUDE.md` now `@AGENTS.md`. Detail: `docs/handoffs/2026-09-14-doctor-plus-context-audit.md`."," - 2026-09-14 migration closed out. Every DEV project repo has a GitHub remote under erash11, all clean and pushed. Duplicate clone folders (`Gemini Projects`, `Website`) moved to `_to_delete/2026-09-14_dup_clones/`."]},{"oldStart":23,"oldLines":6,"newStart":31,"newLines":8,"lines":[" - Baylor's 2026 forecast snapshot is frozen at 4.49 expected wins."," "," ## Next","+- Windows: restart RStudio before the next `Football/SpeedProfiling` session, so it picks up `RENV_PATHS_LIBRARY_ROOT` and does not rebuild the renv library inside DEV.","+- Windows: recheck the Google Drive error count (expect 2, was 162). Quit and reopen Drive to force a rescan."," - Next session: confirm every listed skill shows a description (skill listing budget is ~30,000 chars; predicted ~26,800)."," - Rotate the exposed VALD client secret, then verify the replacement is stored outside Git and project documentation."," - Delete `~/Documents/Codex` when ready. 3.2 GB, nothing in it that is not already in git."]},{"oldStart":39,"oldLines":6,"newStart":49,"newLines":10,"lines":[" - `LibraryProject.code-workspace` points at a nonexistent nested `SportScienceResearchRepo`; the live repo is at the DEV root."," "," ## Gotchas","+- Worktree folders and `.git/worktrees/` metadata fail to delete with `Permission denied` because **Google Drive for Desktop holds them open**, not because of privileges — no elevated shell needed. Quit Drive (Pause is not enough), then delete. PowerShell `Remove-Item -Recurse -Force` run from a directory outside the target works where Git Bash `rm -rf` reports `Device or resource busy` (Bash refuses while its own cwd is inside). All stubs were cleared this way on 09-22, including the old `router-wrr` and `router+dexa-windows-path`.","+- A leftover worktree branch is not automatically junk. Run `git log origin/main..<branch>` before deleting: `status+closeout-0917` held the only copy of the 09-17 DexaProject handoff (recovered 09-22).","+- Comparing a Windows checkout against a Mac-authored copy: normalize line endings before concluding the two have diverged. Raw md5s made six identical DexaProject files look different on 09-17. Binary files are the reliable signal.","+- `DexaProject` is no longer in `~/DEV` on either machine. It lives only on Google Drive — Windows `G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive\\DexaProject`. Identifiable health data; never paste its contents anywhere."," - `skillOverrides` does not apply to plugin skills. A plugin is on or off as a whole."," - `~/.agents/skills` and `~/.codex/skills` are generated views, not authoring locations. Edit and push `~/.claude/skills`, then run the platform sync; do not hand-edit managed copies."," - The top-level `ZoteroInjestion` checkout is the working clone. `LibraryProject` carries the same repo as a submodule and currently pins the same `10e3986` commit; later Zotero commits require a submodule-pointer bump there."]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/docs/handoffs/2026-09-17-dexaproject-windows-removal.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":87,"lines":["+# 2026-09-17 — DexaProject removed from Windows `~/DEV`; router records both Drive paths","+","+## What this was","+","+`DexaProject/` holds identifiable DEXA health data. The Mac moved it out of `~/DEV` to Google","+Drive on 2026-09-09, and both router files were updated then to say it no longer lives in `~/DEV`.","+","+On the Windows laptop the directory was still sitting in the DEV root. The router was therefore","+**false on this machine** — it asserted a state that held on one machine only. This session","+removed the Windows copy and updated the router to carry each machine's path to the one Drive","+folder.","+","+## Why it was safe to delete","+","+The deletion was only safe because the Drive copy provably superseded the local one. Verified","+before touching anything:","+","+- `git merge-base --is-ancestor` — Drive HEAD `5ab14b6` is a **descendant** of the local HEAD","+  `962ce2d`. The Drive repo contained all 4 local commits plus 2 more (`Ignore .DS_Store`,","+  `Merge GitHub scaffolding before deleting the remote`).","+- Local working tree clean, no stashes, no branches beyond `main`.","+- The `.mdb` database **byte-identical** on both sides (`ec327cd257acc28f8c1fda98a01218f6`).","+- The 3 CSVs and the markdown files differed **only in CRLF vs LF**. Raw md5s made them look","+  diverged; normalizing line endings showed them identical. Do not trust a bare hash comparison","+  between a Windows checkout and a Mac-authored copy.","+- The one genuine difference, `.gitignore`, is the Mac's deliberate change — it kept the original","+  as `.gitignore.from-github`.","+","+No data was copied anywhere. The Drive folder was never written to; only the redundant Windows","+copy was removed.","+","+## Decisions and their reasoning","+","+- **Deleted outright rather than moved to the Recycle Bin or `_ARCHIVE/`.** A lingering second","+  copy of identifiable health data is worse than none, and the content is fully recoverable from","+  the Drive copy's git history. `_ARCHIVE/` would also have kept it inside `~/DEV`, which is the","+  exact thing the move exists to prevent.","+- **Recorded both machines' paths instead of replacing the Mac's.** One Drive folder, two path","+  spellings. Replacing the Mac path would have made the router false on the Mac — the same bug","+  in the other direction.","+- **Backup manifest left unedited.** `daily-backup.ps1` reads `backup-manifest.json`, whose","+  `paths[]` is machine-neutral; `backup-manifest.windows.json` is a destinations-only overlay","+  that nothing reads yet. The manifest's only `DexaProject` entry is the Mac Drive path,","+  SSD-destination-only, and is still correct.","+- **Did NOT claim the Windows copy was tripping the manifest's default-deny rule.** An earlier","+  draft of PR #2 asserted this; the log does not support it. `DexaProject` appears in","+  `daily-backup.log` only in the inverse direction — as a *declared* dir absent from disk — and","+  never in an `unmanaged` list, and that log's last entry is 2026-08-14. The claim was corrected","+  before merge.","+","+## Files created or modified","+","+- **Deleted:** `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\DexaProject` (60 files including `.git`)","+- **Deleted:** `~/.claude/global-memory/dev-docs/DexaProject/` — orphaned docs mirror; the","+  harvest script copies `docs/*.md` but never prunes, so a removed repo's mirror outlives it","+- **Modified:** `~/DEV/CLAUDE.md` — \"Handling care\" now lists Mac and Windows paths","+- **Modified:** `~/DEV/PERFORMANCE.md` — row records both paths and both move dates","+- **Modified:** `~/.claude/global-memory/handoffs/2026-09-17-windows-sync-vault-path-fix.md` —","+  items #1 and #2 marked done","+- **Sole remaining copy:** `G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive\\DexaProject` — HEAD `5ab14b6`,","+  11 files, clean","+","+Commits: `c56e1a5` (router), merged to `main` as `cb6c3f2` via PR #2. Global-memory `d7a5a3b`,","+`0d54622`, `79a3f0d`. Dotclaude `198a43d`, `164db21`.","+","+## Next actions","+","+1. **Nothing outstanding on the move itself.** It is complete and verified on both sides.","+2. `PERFORMANCE.md` still describes the folder as \"Not in git, not pushed anywhere.\" The Drive","+   copy does carry a `.git` with 6 commits and a dead `remotes/gh/main` remote. **\"Not on","+   GitHub\" is the accurate phrasing** — flagged in PR #2, deliberately not changed unilaterally.","+3. The Drive copy's `.gitignore` no longer covers `.env` (the Mac replaced it with a one-line","+   `.DS_Store` file). Harmless for a repo that is never pushed; restore if you want the","+   belt-and-braces.","+4. `router/weekly-research-review` is a leftover merged local branch from PR #1, safe to delete.","+","+## Gotchas for the next session","+","+- **`.git/worktrees/` metadata cannot be deleted on this machine.** `git worktree remove` and","+  `git worktree prune` both fail with `Permission denied`, leaving stubs (`ORIG_HEAD`, `logs/`,","+  `refs/`). Two now exist: `router-wrr` (since 09-16) and `router+dexa-windows-path`. Git no","+  longer tracks either — `git worktree list` shows only `main` — so they are cosmetic, but they","+  print an error on every prune and fetch. Two separate worktrees failing identically points at","+  a file lock or an AD permission quirk, not chance. Deleting them needs an elevated shell.","+- **Windows-vs-Mac file comparison:** always normalize line endings before concluding two copies","+  have diverged. Binary files (`.mdb`) are the reliable signal.","+- The DEV repo now discovers **143** repos, not 144."]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/docs/handoffs/2026-09-22-worktree-cleanup-renv-drive-tos-scaffold.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":87,"lines":["+# Handoff — 2026-09-22 — Worktree cleanup, renv moved out of DEV, TOS scaffold","+","+Windows laptop, Claude Code background session. Picked up from the two 2026-09-21 handoffs","+(`global-memory/handoffs/2026-09-21-mac-owns-data-pulls.md` and `-windows-devsync-pulls-to-mac.md`)","+and closed out their Windows-side open items.","+","+## Eric's decisions this session","+","+- **No `pmset` wake on the Mac.** Afternoon pulls may run late when the Mac sleeps. Accepted.","+- **Credential rotation (VALD client secret, Catapult token) stays deferred.** Not urgent; repos are private.","+- **`DEV/AthleticMedicineReviews/Report_help.zip` stays as is.** Not opened, not put in a repo.","+- **Google Drive keeps backing up `Desktop\\DEV`.** It is the only backup of several GB of local-only","+  data (`Risk_Stratification_Engine/outputs` 1.8 GB, `Football/SpeedProfiling/data` 1.7 GB,","+  `ForcePlate_DecisionSystem/data` 1.6 GB). The long-term fix, not done: move data that cannot be","+  regenerated to `G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive` and stop backing up DEV.","+- **The `gh pr merge` auto-mode rule was approved and added by Eric himself.** Claude's own edit to","+  `~/.claude/settings.json` was refused twice by the self-modification guard even with approval.","+  If a future session needs a settings change, expect to hand Eric the text to paste.","+","+## Google Drive sync errors: cause and fix","+","+162 Drive errors, all the same cause: Drive for Desktop cannot open a Windows **junction**, so each one","+logs `PERMISSION_DENIED: CreateFileW failed` (`local_disk_bridge.cc:1414`) forever.","+","+- 160 were `Football/SpeedProfiling/renv/library/windows/R-4.5/x86_64-w64-mingw32/<pkg>`, every one a","+  junction into renv's shared cache at `AppData\\Local\\R\\cache\\R\\renv\\cache\\v5`.","+- 2 are `DEV\\_DRIVE` (→ `G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive`) and","+  `DEV\\LibraryProject\\ZoteroInjestion` (→ `DEV\\ZoteroInjestion`). Kept on purpose, so 2 errors are expected.","+","+Fix applied: user env var `RENV_PATHS_LIBRARY_ROOT` = `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\AppData\\Local\\R\\renv-library`","+(set with `[Environment]::SetEnvironmentVariable(...,'User')` — `setx` with `%LOCALAPPDATA%` stores the","+literal string and R will not expand it). Then `renv::restore(prompt = FALSE)` in SpeedProfiling rebuilt","+the library at `...\\renv-library\\SpeedProfiling-e6898666\\windows\\R-4.5\\x86_64-w64-mingw32` (161 packages,","+`renv::status()` synchronized). The 160 junctions were unlinked with","+`[System.IO.Directory]::Delete(path, false)` so the shared cache was untouched (163 cache dirs before and","+after), then `renv/library` was removed from the repo. **Restart RStudio** before working in SpeedProfiling;","+a process started before the env var was set would rebuild the library inside DEV and bring the errors back.","+","+## Worktree cleanup (4 + 1)","+","+Deleted: `_INBOX/.claude/worktrees/{mac-owns-pulls,task-disabled}` and","+`DataBase_GPS_Reporting/.claude/worktrees/{mac-owns-pulls,coach-report}`, plus their `.git/worktrees/`","+metadata, and the merged branches `refresh-task-disabled-0921`, `coach-report-v2`, `coach-report`","+(local and GitHub). Every one verified clean and fully merged first.","+","+`DEV/.claude/worktrees/status+closeout-0917` was **not** disposable: it held one unmerged commit","+(`d248049`, 09-17) with `docs/handoffs/2026-09-17-dexaproject-windows-removal.md` (87 lines) that existed","+nowhere else, and STATUS entries main never had. Its PR (#3) had sat open since 09-17 and conflicted.","+Resolved `docs/STATUS.md` by keeping both dated entries, merged as `bb266b9`, then cleared.","+","+**Lesson worth keeping:** a leftover worktree is not automatically junk. Check","+`git log origin/main..<branch>` before deleting one; this one was two commands away from losing a handoff.","+","+## Gotchas hit","+","+- Google Drive holds worktree files open: `git worktree remove` and `rm -rf` both fail with","+  `Permission denied`. Quitting Drive (not pausing) released them. PowerShell `Remove-Item` from a","+  directory outside the target also succeeded where Git Bash `rm -rf` reported `Device or resource busy`","+  — Bash was refusing because its own cwd was inside the tree.","+- `DataBase_GPS_Reporting` had `.claude/worktrees/coach-report` **tracked** in git even though","+  `.gitignore` lists it. Deleting the folder left a staged deletion to commit.","+- A worktree-isolated session refuses compound git commands and `sed` with runtime-computed arguments.","+  Split into plain, separate commands.","+","+## Files created or modified","+","+- `DEV/TOS_Evidence_Brief/`: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `docs/STATUS.md`, `.gitignore` (PR #1, merged `30be306`)","+- `DEV/RESEARCH.md`: TOS_Evidence_Brief row (PR #5, merged `ecc13b2`)","+- `DEV/docs/STATUS.md` + `docs/handoffs/2026-09-17-dexaproject-windows-removal.md` (recovered, PR #3, `bb266b9`)","+- `DEV/docs/STATUS.md` and this handoff (this closeout)","+- `DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting`: stale `.claude/worktrees/coach-report` entry removed","+- `DEV/Football/SpeedProfiling/renv/library/` deleted (library moved out of DEV)","+- `~/.claude/settings.json`: `autoMode.allow` gh pr merge rule (Eric added; commit `9b6d047`, pushed)","+- `~/.claude/machine.md`: renv/Drive junction trap + Rscript path (gitignored, Windows-only)","+","+## Next actions","+","+1. Restart RStudio before the next SpeedProfiling session (see above).","+2. Check the Drive error count later; it updates on rescan. Expect 2, not 162. Quit and reopen Drive to force it.","+3. `ForcePlate_DecisionSystem`: add scipy to requirements (`tests/test_heterogeneity.py` needs it). Optional.","+4. Have `claude-stack-doctor` read the three pull receipts. Optional.","+5. Still deferred by Eric: rotate the VALD client secret and the Catapult token.","+","+## Mid-flight","+","+Nothing running. `PT_Dash` sits on branch `claude/cmj-performance-report-011CURrnCVZRnL3cTVQHoiGN` and","+`Football/SpeedProfiling` on `add-2025-smu`; both are clean and pushed, and neither was touched today."]}],"created":true}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kristinarash/DEV/PLATFORM.md","/Users/kristinarash/DEV/RESEARCH.md","/Users/kristinarash/DEV/docs/STATUS.md","/Users/kristinarash/DEV/docs/handoffs/2026-09-17-dexaproject-windows-removal.md","/Users/kristinarash/DEV/docs/handoffs/2026-09-22-worktree-cleanup-renv-drive-tos-scaffold.md"]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c78245fc-f9bc-4416-a2b4-b45c6126d162","session_id":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","version":"2.1.280","gitBranch":"main"}
