{"parentUuid":"6598ce74-0499-4d0e-bc9b-ae68943290a9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"87d6c547-b2ad-4d4f-b4f7-18e6b02e26a7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 1\n# PFF Data Project — Agent Guide\n\nThis file is the canonical project memory for any AI coding agent working in this\nrepo. It is mirrored verbatim into `AGENTS.md` so OpenAI Codex (and any other\nagent that reads `AGENTS.md`) gets the same context. A pre-commit hook in\n`.githooks/pre-commit` blocks commits where the two files diverge.\n\nIf you edit one, edit both. See \"Keeping CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md in sync\" below.\n\n---\n\n## What this project is\n\nA standalone Python data pipeline that pulls Pro Football Focus (PFF) game and\nplayer data into a local **DuckDB** database for Baylor University Football\nanalysis. Scope is **Baylor + every Big 12 team + non-conference opponents** for\nthe **current season plus two prior**.\n\nThe DB *is* the deliverable. There are no dashboards in this repo. Downstream\nconsumers — Power BI, Jupyter notebooks, and a future athlete management system\n(AMS) project that will unify PFF with Catapult GPS, VALD ForceDecks, and Perch\nVBT data — own visualization and cross-domain joins.\n\n## Sister pipelines (do not modify from here)\n\n- **VALD ForceDecks (CMJ/IMTP):** `..\\..\\ForcePlate_DecisionSystem` — the\n  architectural template this project mirrors.\n- **Catapult GPS:** `..\\..\\DataBase_GPS_Reporting`\n- **Perch VBT:** not yet built.\n\nThe pattern across all of them is: per-domain Python pipeline → per-domain DB →\nfuture AMS layer unions them on `(athlete_id, source_system, pulled_at)`.\n\n## Tech stack\n\n- Python 3.12+\n- `duckdb`, `requests`, `python-dotenv`, `PyJWT`, `pyyaml`, `pandas`, `pytest`\n- No web framework, no ORM, no dashboard libs — keep it lean\n\n## Layout\n\n```\nPFF_Data_Project/\n├── CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md       # this file (mirrored)\n├── README.md                   # user-facing setup and usage\n├── requirements.txt\n├── .env.example                # PFF_BASE_URL, PFF_API_KEY, BAYLOR_TEAM_ID\n├── .gitignore\n├── .githooks/pre-commit        # blocks CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md divergence\n├── run_pipeline.py             # CLI entry\n├── config/\n│   └── pipeline.yaml           # team/season scope, endpoints, retry config\n├── src/\n│   ├── db.py                   # DuckDB schema + connect + backup helpers\n│   ├── ingest/\n│   │   ├── pff_client.py       # PFF HTTP client (stub until Phase 0 done)\n│   │   └── pipeline.py         # Orchestration: dims → facts → log\n│   └── shape/transform.py      # JSON → tidy rows (teams/games/grades/stats/premium)\n├── data/                       # small extracts only; the DuckDB lives at $PFF_DB\n├── docs/\n(eval):1: ===== not found","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D26wWTZjPPMS3quiPSgTAD"}]},"uuid":"23dc4d48-0cc0-4d71-a145-1109c5a54d98","timestamp":"2026-09-22T22:51:41.815Z","toolUseResult":"Error: Exit code 1\n# PFF Data Project — Agent Guide\n\nThis file is the canonical project memory for any AI coding agent working in this\nrepo. It is mirrored verbatim into `AGENTS.md` so OpenAI Codex (and any other\nagent that reads `AGENTS.md`) gets the same context. A pre-commit hook in\n`.githooks/pre-commit` blocks commits where the two files diverge.\n\nIf you edit one, edit both. See \"Keeping CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md in sync\" below.\n\n---\n\n## What this project is\n\nA standalone Python data pipeline that pulls Pro Football Focus (PFF) game and\nplayer data into a local **DuckDB** database for Baylor University Football\nanalysis. Scope is **Baylor + every Big 12 team + non-conference opponents** for\nthe **current season plus two prior**.\n\nThe DB *is* the deliverable. There are no dashboards in this repo. Downstream\nconsumers — Power BI, Jupyter notebooks, and a future athlete management system\n(AMS) project that will unify PFF with Catapult GPS, VALD ForceDecks, and Perch\nVBT data — own visualization and cross-domain joins.\n\n## Sister pipelines (do not modify from here)\n\n- **VALD ForceDecks (CMJ/IMTP):** `..\\..\\ForcePlate_DecisionSystem` — the\n  architectural template this project mirrors.\n- **Catapult GPS:** `..\\..\\DataBase_GPS_Reporting`\n- **Perch VBT:** not yet built.\n\nThe pattern across all of them is: per-domain Python pipeline → per-domain DB →\nfuture AMS layer unions them on `(athlete_id, source_system, pulled_at)`.\n\n## Tech stack\n\n- Python 3.12+\n- `duckdb`, `requests`, `python-dotenv`, `PyJWT`, `pyyaml`, `pandas`, `pytest`\n- No web framework, no ORM, no dashboard libs — keep it lean\n\n## Layout\n\n```\nPFF_Data_Project/\n├── CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md       # this file (mirrored)\n├── README.md                   # user-facing setup and usage\n├── requirements.txt\n├── .env.example                # PFF_BASE_URL, PFF_API_KEY, BAYLOR_TEAM_ID\n├── .gitignore\n├── .githooks/pre-commit        # blocks CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md divergence\n├── run_pipeline.py             # CLI entry\n├── config/\n│   └── pipeline.yaml           # team/season scope, endpoints, retry config\n├── src/\n│   ├── db.py                   # DuckDB schema + connect + backup helpers\n│   ├── ingest/\n│   │   ├── pff_client.py       # PFF HTTP client (stub until Phase 0 done)\n│   │   └── pipeline.py         # Orchestration: dims → facts → log\n│   └── shape/transform.py      # JSON → tidy rows (teams/games/grades/stats/premium)\n├── data/                       # small extracts only; the DuckDB lives at $PFF_DB\n├── docs/\n(eval):1: ===== not found","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6598ce74-0499-4d0e-bc9b-ae68943290a9","session_id":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project","sessionId":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","version":"2.1.280","gitBranch":"main"}
