{"parentUuid":"d842e5f8-657c-46cd-a431-4c7864254b50","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"skill_listing","content":"- anthropic-skills:closeout: End-of-session sign-off ritual. Sweeps loose ends, commits and pushes what needs it, verifies memory capture, writes a cross-harness handoff, and reports \"clear to sign off\" or what's still open. Use when the user says \"/closeout\", \"any loose ends?\", \"am I good to sign off?\", \"close out for the night\", \"closing out\", \"goodnight\", \"wrap up for the day\", or asks for a system health check before leaving. Do not use at the start of a session (use startup) or for a standalone automation health check (use claude-stack-doctor).\n- anthropic-skills:dev-sync: Bring this machine into line with GitHub and load back the context that came with it: locate DEV automatically, pull config and skills, inventory every project, commit and push local work, pull the other machine's work, clone what is missing, report conflicts, then read the repo's STATUS and latest handoff and report where the last session left off. Use when Eric switches machines, sits down to start work, says 'sync DEV', asks whether everything is pushed, or asks where he left off. Do not use when Eric says '/startup' or 'good morning' (use startup, which runs this sync) or to scaffold a new repo (use new-project).\n- anthropic-skills:new-project: Scaffold a new project in DEV the standard way: git repo, AGENTS.md with the session routine, CLAUDE.md pointer, docs/STATUS.md, .gitignore, private GitHub repo under erash11. Use when Eric starts a new project or says 'set this up as a repo'. Do not use to log an idea in the portfolio registry (use project) or to sync repos that already exist (use dev-sync).","skillCount":3,"isInitial":false,"names":["anthropic-skills:closeout","anthropic-skills:dev-sync","anthropic-skills:new-project"]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b91906fa-6a80-4718-be21-8995dabb6dfe","timestamp":"2026-09-22T23:20:07.539Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nThe following skills are available for use with the Skill tool:\n\n- anthropic-skills:closeout: End-of-session sign-off ritual. Sweeps loose ends, commits and pushes what needs it, verifies memory capture, writes a cross-harness handoff, and reports \"clear to sign off\" or what's still open. Use when the user says \"/closeout\", \"any loose ends?\", \"am I good to sign off?\", \"close out for the night\", \"closing out\", \"goodnight\", \"wrap up for the day\", or asks for a system health check before leaving. Do not use at the start of a session (use startup) or for a standalone automation health check (use claude-stack-doctor).\n- anthropic-skills:dev-sync: Bring this machine into line with GitHub and load back the context that came with it: locate DEV automatically, pull config and skills, inventory every project, commit and push local work, pull the other machine's work, clone what is missing, report conflicts, then read the repo's STATUS and latest handoff and report where the last session left off. Use when Eric switches machines, sits down to start work, says 'sync DEV', asks whether everything is pushed, or asks where he left off. Do not use when Eric says '/startup' or 'good morning' (use startup, which runs this sync) or to scaffold a new repo (use new-project).\n- anthropic-skills:new-project: Scaffold a new project in DEV the standard way: git repo, AGENTS.md with the session routine, CLAUDE.md pointer, docs/STATUS.md, .gitignore, private GitHub repo under erash11. Use when Eric starts a new project or says 'set this up as a repo'. Do not use to log an idea in the portfolio registry (use project) or to sync repos that already exist (use dev-sync).\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project","sessionId":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","version":"2.1.280","gitBranch":"main"}
