{"parentUuid":"c362eaaa-fdfd-4889-b863-695ec77cfcd4","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0aa7bf31-cb90-46db-810d-7f68a7e97430","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F8zP4vjdbU74iKS5bBofV2","type":"tool_result","content":"9d46de6 2026-09-22 17:51:57 -0500 Closeout 2026-09-22: STATUS current state, handoff for the DB move and snapshots (#3)\nf8e3d78 2026-09-13 22:20:18 -0500 Closeout 2026-09-13: STATUS next, open questions, gotchas\n6cfed01 2026-09-13 21:51:24 -0500 Docs: season video-plays pull and its dtype trap\n# STATUS\n\n## Current state (2026-09-22)\n- **The DB no longer lives in the repo.** `src/db.py` resolves it from **`$PFF_DB`**\n  (Windows: `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\pff-data\\pff.db`), falling back to `data/pff.db` when unset,\n  so the Mac is unchanged until it sets the variable. Cause: `~/Desktop/DEV` is a two-way\n  Google Drive mirror and Drive re-uploads and **locks** the 542 MB file on every write.\n  `GoogleDriveFS.exe` held it open against a running pull. PR #1.\n- **2026 pulled** (`run_pipeline.py --season 2026`): 1,614 games, 16,572 grades,\n  1,252,863 stats, 39,960 premium; graded weeks 0-3. Baylor: 79 players over its 3\n  played games, 17,215 snaps. Week 4 is 2026-09-26, so 3 games is complete, not a gap.\n- **Machines now exchange Parquet, not databases** (PR #2). `scripts/export_snapshot.py`\n  and `scripts/load_snapshot.py`, one file per table per season on Drive plus a\n  manifest. The whole 612 MB DB is **40 MB** of Parquet; all of 2026 is 6 MB. A full\n  snapshot of 2023-2026 is on Drive now, so the Mac can catch up without touching the API.\n\n## Done\n- Repo brought under git and pushed to erash11 (2026-09-09).\n- All 12 PFF API specs saved to `docs/swagger/` (2026-09-13). Eight were new; master-data\n  and grades-feeds were refreshed (both only gained endpoints). The key downloads specs\n  directly: `GET /doc/swagger/<slug>.yaml` with the Bearer JWT.\n- PFF EPA located and verified (2026-09-13): `/v1/video/ncaa/games/{id}/plays` carries\n  `expected_points_added` and `expected_points_added_legacy`, 100% play coverage on\n  Baylor 2024-2026 and six random non-Baylor 2025 games.\n- Video plays ingested for all 25 Baylor 2024-2025 games (2026-09-13): `pff_premium`\n  category `video_plays`, 4,517 rows (both offences), zero missing EPA.\n  `scripts/pull_video_plays.py --season 2024 --season 2025`. Season and week come\n  from the games table: a bowl game's rows carry week \"BG\". Pre-change backup:\n  `data/pff_before_video_plays_20260913_204343.db`.\n- Full 2024 and 2025 seasons pulled (2026-09-13): 285,070 and 290,427 plays plus the","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a05536b8-cea4-4151-888f-2573bd74ed09","timestamp":"2026-09-22T23:22:54.716Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"9d46de6 2026-09-22 17:51:57 -0500 Closeout 2026-09-22: STATUS current state, handoff for the DB move and snapshots (#3)\nf8e3d78 2026-09-13 22:20:18 -0500 Closeout 2026-09-13: STATUS next, open questions, gotchas\n6cfed01 2026-09-13 21:51:24 -0500 Docs: season video-plays pull and its dtype trap\n# STATUS\n\n## Current state (2026-09-22)\n- **The DB no longer lives in the repo.** `src/db.py` resolves it from **`$PFF_DB`**\n  (Windows: `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\pff-data\\pff.db`), falling back to `data/pff.db` when unset,\n  so the Mac is unchanged until it sets the variable. Cause: `~/Desktop/DEV` is a two-way\n  Google Drive mirror and Drive re-uploads and **locks** the 542 MB file on every write.\n  `GoogleDriveFS.exe` held it open against a running pull. PR #1.\n- **2026 pulled** (`run_pipeline.py --season 2026`): 1,614 games, 16,572 grades,\n  1,252,863 stats, 39,960 premium; graded weeks 0-3. Baylor: 79 players over its 3\n  played games, 17,215 snaps. Week 4 is 2026-09-26, so 3 games is complete, not a gap.\n- **Machines now exchange Parquet, not databases** (PR #2). `scripts/export_snapshot.py`\n  and `scripts/load_snapshot.py`, one file per table per season on Drive plus a\n  manifest. The whole 612 MB DB is **40 MB** of Parquet; all of 2026 is 6 MB. A full\n  snapshot of 2023-2026 is on Drive now, so the Mac can catch up without touching the API.\n\n## Done\n- Repo brought under git and pushed to erash11 (2026-09-09).\n- All 12 PFF API specs saved to `docs/swagger/` (2026-09-13). Eight were new; master-data\n  and grades-feeds were refreshed (both only gained endpoints). The key downloads specs\n  directly: `GET /doc/swagger/<slug>.yaml` with the Bearer JWT.\n- PFF EPA located and verified (2026-09-13): `/v1/video/ncaa/games/{id}/plays` carries\n  `expected_points_added` and `expected_points_added_legacy`, 100% play coverage on\n  Baylor 2024-2026 and six random non-Baylor 2025 games.\n- Video plays ingested for all 25 Baylor 2024-2025 games (2026-09-13): `pff_premium`\n  category `video_plays`, 4,517 rows (both offences), zero missing EPA.\n  `scripts/pull_video_plays.py --season 2024 --season 2025`. Season and week come\n  from the games table: a bowl game's rows carry week \"BG\". Pre-change backup:\n  `data/pff_before_video_plays_20260913_204343.db`.\n- Full 2024 and 2025 seasons pulled (2026-09-13): 285,070 and 290,427 plays plus the","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c362eaaa-fdfd-4889-b863-695ec77cfcd4","session_id":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project","sessionId":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","version":"2.1.280","gitBranch":"main"}
