{"parentUuid":"efdfa2c6-dbd1-4982-953f-7b568756338e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0aa7bf31-cb90-46db-810d-7f68a7e97430","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U46jr3Z5H4LuHEq5HfFBwY","type":"tool_result","content":"- Full 2024 and 2025 seasons pulled (2026-09-13): 285,070 and 290,427 plays plus the\n  games lists, `scripts/pull_season_video_plays.py`. Verified against the per-game pull\n  (all 2,215 Baylor plays identical). Current equals legacy on 1.7% of plays, so the\n  2024 model backfill happened. Consumed by PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA Phase 7.\n\n- EPA source comparison done 2026-09-13 in PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA (Phases 6 and 7).\n  Decision (Eric): EPA (PFF current) is the EPA source going forward.\n\n## Next\n1. **On the Mac:** `git pull`, then `python scripts/load_snapshot.py` to take the 2026\n   season from Drive. Do not re-pull it from the API. Setting `$PFF_DB` there is\n   optional; unset keeps the Mac's existing path.\n2. Pull 2026 weekly with `scripts/pull_season_video_plays.py --season 2026 --refresh`, so\n   MatchupAnalysis opponent profiles can quote EPA (PFF current) instead of CFBD PPA.\n   **Video plays are still Mac-only on this box** - the 09-13 ingests never reached\n   Windows, and `load_snapshot.py` moves them once the Mac exports.\n3. Re-run `--season 2026` weekly during the season; each run adds the graded week.\n4. After the 2026 season, a full 2026 pull for the PlayCalls Phase 7 rerun.\n\n## Open questions\n- None waiting on Eric.\n\n## Gotchas\n- The season feed is about 2.5 GB decoded; stream it (ijson), never `response.json()`.\n- `season_plays.to_frame` needs `dtype=object`, or gappy int columns land as `\"2.0\"`/`\"nan\"`.\n- Bowl-week rows carry week \"BG\"; take season and week from the games list.\n\n---\n\n## Merged from windows copy (2026-09-11)\n\n<!-- Contents of STATUS.md.from-windows, kept verbatim so nothing is lost. Fold into the sections above when convenient. -->\n\n# STATUS\n\nRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\n## Current state\n- Snapshot committed 2026-09-09 during migration to the DEV + GitHub workflow.\n\n## Next\n-\n\n## Open questions\n-\n\n## Gotchas\n-","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"95c7828d-efc1-4899-b12c-6d417eb49cc9","timestamp":"2026-09-22T23:22:57.475Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"- Full 2024 and 2025 seasons pulled (2026-09-13): 285,070 and 290,427 plays plus the\n  games lists, `scripts/pull_season_video_plays.py`. Verified against the per-game pull\n  (all 2,215 Baylor plays identical). Current equals legacy on 1.7% of plays, so the\n  2024 model backfill happened. Consumed by PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA Phase 7.\n\n- EPA source comparison done 2026-09-13 in PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA (Phases 6 and 7).\n  Decision (Eric): EPA (PFF current) is the EPA source going forward.\n\n## Next\n1. **On the Mac:** `git pull`, then `python scripts/load_snapshot.py` to take the 2026\n   season from Drive. Do not re-pull it from the API. Setting `$PFF_DB` there is\n   optional; unset keeps the Mac's existing path.\n2. Pull 2026 weekly with `scripts/pull_season_video_plays.py --season 2026 --refresh`, so\n   MatchupAnalysis opponent profiles can quote EPA (PFF current) instead of CFBD PPA.\n   **Video plays are still Mac-only on this box** - the 09-13 ingests never reached\n   Windows, and `load_snapshot.py` moves them once the Mac exports.\n3. Re-run `--season 2026` weekly during the season; each run adds the graded week.\n4. After the 2026 season, a full 2026 pull for the PlayCalls Phase 7 rerun.\n\n## Open questions\n- None waiting on Eric.\n\n## Gotchas\n- The season feed is about 2.5 GB decoded; stream it (ijson), never `response.json()`.\n- `season_plays.to_frame` needs `dtype=object`, or gappy int columns land as `\"2.0\"`/`\"nan\"`.\n- Bowl-week rows carry week \"BG\"; take season and week from the games list.\n\n---\n\n## Merged from windows copy (2026-09-11)\n\n<!-- Contents of STATUS.md.from-windows, kept verbatim so nothing is lost. Fold into the sections above when convenient. -->\n\n# STATUS\n\nRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\n## Current state\n- Snapshot committed 2026-09-09 during migration to the DEV + GitHub workflow.\n\n## Next\n-\n\n## Open questions\n-\n\n## Gotchas\n-","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"efdfa2c6-dbd1-4982-953f-7b568756338e","session_id":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project","sessionId":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","version":"2.1.280","gitBranch":"main"}
