{"parentUuid":"6e188819-a56c-445f-bed9-4563fa071576","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfKLdaW3JxFuwMYbWqwLD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015rLa56HkFNhY5kFcp597T1","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project && python3 - <<'EOF'\np=\"docs/STATUS.md\"; s=open(p).read()\nold_next=s[s.index(\"1. **On the Mac:**\"):s.index(\"2. Pull 2026 weekly\")]\nnew_next=\"\"\"1. **Fix `load_snapshot.py` before anyone loads again.** It deletes a whole season, then\n   inserts only what the snapshot has. On 2026-09-22 the Mac load erased 12,750 Mac-only\n   `pff_premium` rows (2024-2025: `video_plays`, `team_play`, `quarterback_charting`,\n   `rushing`). They were restored from the pre-load backup the same night. Fix idea:\n   replace per (season, category) for `pff_premium`, or refuse when local has a category\n   the snapshot lacks. See `docs/handoffs/2026-09-22-mac-snapshot-load-restore.md`.\n2. **Then export from the Mac** (`python scripts/export_snapshot.py --season 2024 --season 2025`)\n   so Windows gets those rows. Until then, **Windows must not export 2024/2025 over them.**\n\"\"\"\ns=s.replace(old_next,new_next).replace(\"2. Pull 2026 weekly\",\"3. Pull 2026 weekly\").replace(\"3. Re-run `--season 2026`\",\"4. Re-run `--season 2026`\").replace(\"4. After the 2026 season\",\"5. After the 2026 season\")\ns=s.replace(\"so the Mac can catch up without touching the API.\\n\",\"so the Mac can catch up without touching the API.\\n- **Mac loaded the snapshot 2026-09-22 18:15** and matches it (22 files, all counts equal;\\n  2026 checked row by row). Load bug found and repaired the same night: see Next 1.\\n\",1)\ns=s.replace(\"## Gotchas\\n\",\"## Gotchas\\n- `load_snapshot.py` is season-scoped: any local row the snapshot lacks for that season is\\n  deleted. Run `--dry-run` AND compare `pff_premium` categories before a real load.\\n- The Mac's plain `python3` has no `duckdb`. Use `~/.local/bin/uv run --with-requirements requirements.txt --with pyarrow python ...`.\\n\",1)\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nEOF\nsed -n 1,50p docs/STATUS.md | grep -n \"Mac loaded\\|Fix \\`load\\|Then export\\|3. Pull\\|season-scoped\"","description":"Update STATUS.md with the load result and bug"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":731,"cache_read_input_tokens":109476,"output_tokens":1105,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":145},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":731,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1105,"cache_read_input_tokens":109476,"cache_creation_input_tokens":731,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":731},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_015rLa56HkFNhY5kFcp597T1":{"command":"cd ~/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project && python3 - <<'EOF'\np=\"docs/STATUS.md\"; s=open(p).read()\nold_next=s[s.index(\"1. **On the Mac:**\"):s.index(\"2. Pull 2026 weekly\")]\nnew_next=\"\"\"1. **Fix `load_snapshot.py` before anyone loads again.** It deletes a whole season, then\n   inserts only what the snapshot has. On 2026-09-22 the Mac load erased 12,750 Mac-only\n   `pff_premium` rows (2024-2025: `video_plays`, `team_play`, `quarterback_charting`,\n   `rushing`). They were restored from the pre-load backup the same night. Fix idea:\n   replace per (season, category) for `pff_premium`, or refuse when local has a category\n   the snapshot lacks. See `docs/handoffs/2026-09-22-mac-snapshot-load-restore.md`.\n2. **Then export from the Mac** (`python scripts/export_snapshot.py --season 2024 --season 2025`)\n   so Windows gets those rows. Until then, **Windows must not export 2024/2025 over them.**\n\"\"\"\ns=s.replace(old_next,new_next).replace(\"2. Pull 2026 weekly\",\"3. Pull 2026 weekly\").replace(\"3. Re-run `--season 2026`\",\"4. Re-run `--season 2026`\").replace(\"4. After the 2026 season\",\"5. After the 2026 season\")\ns=s.replace(\"so the Mac can catch up without touching the API.\\n\",\"so the Mac can catch up without touching the API.\\n- **Mac loaded the snapshot 2026-09-22 18:15** and matches it (22 files, all counts equal;\\n  2026 checked row by row). Load bug found and repaired the same night: see Next 1.\\n\",1)\ns=s.replace(\"## Gotchas\\n\",\"## Gotchas\\n- `load_snapshot.py` is season-scoped: any local row the snapshot lacks for that season is\\n  deleted. Run `--dry-run` AND compare `pff_premium` categories before a real load.\\n- The Mac's plain `python3` has no `duckdb`. Use `~/.local/bin/uv run --with-requirements requirements.txt --with pyarrow python ...`.\\n\",1)\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nEOF\nsed -n 1,50p docs/STATUS.md | grep -n \"Mac loaded\\|Fix \\`load\\|Then export\\|3. Pull\\|season-scoped\"","description":"Update STATUS.md with the load result and bug"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfKLdZzn2rwdiGduj1TRJ","attributionSkill":"closeout","type":"assistant","uuid":"14b620ac-8834-47d0-b704-ed937b7b5c57","timestamp":"2026-09-22T23:23:42.416Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project/data","sessionId":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","version":"2.1.280","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"14b620ac-8834-47d0-b704-ed937b7b5c57","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0aa7bf31-cb90-46db-810d-7f68a7e97430","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015rLa56HkFNhY5kFcp597T1","type":"tool_result","content":"16:- **Mac loaded the snapshot 2026-09-22 18:15** and matches it (22 files, all counts equal;\n41:1. **Fix `load_snapshot.py` before anyone loads again.** It deletes a whole season, then\n47:2. **Then export from the Mac** (`python scripts/export_snapshot.py --season 2024 --season 2025`)\n49:3. Pull 2026 weekly with `scripts/pull_season_video_plays.py --season 2026 --refresh`, so","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f37e1f38-035b-44a9-b202-f0a771bf2a56","timestamp":"2026-09-22T23:23:42.728Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"16:- **Mac loaded the snapshot 2026-09-22 18:15** and matches it (22 files, all counts equal;\n41:1. **Fix `load_snapshot.py` before anyone loads again.** It deletes a whole season, then\n47:2. **Then export from the Mac** (`python scripts/export_snapshot.py --season 2024 --season 2025`)\n49:3. Pull 2026 weekly with `scripts/pull_season_video_plays.py --season 2026 --refresh`, so","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project/docs/STATUS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":13,"oldLines":6,"newStart":13,"newLines":8,"lines":["   and `scripts/load_snapshot.py`, one file per table per season on Drive plus a","   manifest. The whole 612 MB DB is **40 MB** of Parquet; all of 2026 is 6 MB. A full","   snapshot of 2023-2026 is on Drive now, so the Mac can catch up without touching the API.","+- **Mac loaded the snapshot 2026-09-22 18:15** and matches it (22 files, all counts equal;","+  2026 checked row by row). Load bug found and repaired the same night: see Next 1."," "," ## Done"," - Repo brought under git and pushed to erash11 (2026-09-09)."]},{"oldStart":36,"oldLines":20,"newStart":38,"newLines":28,"lines":["   Decision (Eric): EPA (PFF current) is the EPA source going forward."," "," ## Next","-1. **On the Mac:** `git pull`, then `python scripts/load_snapshot.py` to take the 2026","-   season from Drive. Do not re-pull it from the API. Setting `$PFF_DB` there is","-   optional; unset keeps the Mac's existing path.","-2. Pull 2026 weekly with `scripts/pull_season_video_plays.py --season 2026 --refresh`, so","+1. **Fix `load_snapshot.py` before anyone loads again.** It deletes a whole season, then","+   inserts only what the snapshot has. On 2026-09-22 the Mac load erased 12,750 Mac-only","+   `pff_premium` rows (2024-2025: `video_plays`, `team_play`, `quarterback_charting`,","+   `rushing`). They were restored from the pre-load backup the same night. Fix idea:","+   replace per (season, category) for `pff_premium`, or refuse when local has a category","+   the snapshot lacks. See `docs/handoffs/2026-09-22-mac-snapshot-load-restore.md`.","+2. **Then export from the Mac** (`python scripts/export_snapshot.py --season 2024 --season 2025`)","+   so Windows gets those rows. Until then, **Windows must not export 2024/2025 over them.**","+3. Pull 2026 weekly with `scripts/pull_season_video_plays.py --season 2026 --refresh`, so","    MatchupAnalysis opponent profiles can quote EPA (PFF current) instead of CFBD PPA.","    **Video plays are still Mac-only on this box** - the 09-13 ingests never reached","    Windows, and `load_snapshot.py` moves them once the Mac exports.","-3. Re-run `--season 2026` weekly during the season; each run adds the graded week.","-4. After the 2026 season, a full 2026 pull for the PlayCalls Phase 7 rerun.","+4. Re-run `--season 2026` weekly during the season; each run adds the graded week.","+5. After the 2026 season, a full 2026 pull for the PlayCalls Phase 7 rerun."," "," ## Open questions"," - None waiting on Eric."," "," ## Gotchas","+- `load_snapshot.py` is season-scoped: any local row the snapshot lacks for that season is","+  deleted. Run `--dry-run` AND compare `pff_premium` categories before a real load.","+- The Mac's plain `python3` has no `duckdb`. Use `~/.local/bin/uv run --with-requirements requirements.txt --with pyarrow python ...`."," - The season feed is about 2.5 GB decoded; stream it (ijson), never `response.json()`."," - `season_plays.to_frame` needs `dtype=object`, or gappy int columns land as `\"2.0\"`/`\"nan\"`."," - Bowl-week rows carry week \"BG\"; take season and week from the games list."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project/docs/STATUS.md"]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"14b620ac-8834-47d0-b704-ed937b7b5c57","session_id":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project","sessionId":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","version":"2.1.280","gitBranch":"main"}
