{"parentUuid":"9ed7512e-3869-4629-b2cf-49e16bf3c1ac","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfKLeKmJ9LtqUsokAU2vd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1403,"cache_read_input_tokens":110207,"output_tokens":1117,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":33},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1403,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1117,"cache_read_input_tokens":110207,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1403,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1403},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfKLeKAq3cJVm6XpfbnKi","attributionSkill":"closeout","type":"assistant","uuid":"e2e4e0e5-7938-47f2-b4e6-d7cd8e0cfdcf","timestamp":"2026-09-22T23:23:44.251Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project","sessionId":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","version":"2.1.280","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"e2e4e0e5-7938-47f2-b4e6-d7cd8e0cfdcf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfKLeKmJ9LtqUsokAU2vd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Gjz42FDRyzn7yPFEJ7LPcH","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project/docs/handoffs/2026-09-22-mac-snapshot-load-restore.md","content":"# 2026-09-22 (Mac, evening): snapshot load, data loss found, rows restored\n\n## What happened\n- Eric ran `scripts/load_snapshot.py` on the Mac at 18:15 to take the Windows export\n  (2023-2026, 22 files, written by BU-1979FJ4 at 22:39 UTC). Backup made by the script:\n  `data/pff_before_load_snapshot_20260922_181535.db`.\n- Verification: `--dry-run` rerun shows all 22 files `same`. 2026 `games`, `pff_grades`,\n  `pff_premium` compared row by row (EXCEPT ALL both ways): 0 differences.\n- **Bug found:** the load deletes each season in the snapshot, then inserts the snapshot's\n  rows. Windows never had the Mac-only `pff_premium` categories, so the Mac lost them:\n\n  | season | category | rows lost |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | 2024 | video_plays | 2,302 |\n  | 2024 | team_play | 2,302 |\n  | 2024 | quarterback_charting | 992 |\n  | 2024 | rushing | 887 |\n  | 2025 | video_plays | 2,215 |\n  | 2025 | team_play | 2,215 |\n  | 2025 | quarterback_charting | 1,014 |\n  | 2025 | rushing | 823 |\n\n- **Restored** the same night: `INSERT INTO pff_premium SELECT * FROM <pre-load backup>`\n  for those 8 (season, category) pairs. The pairs were empty before the insert (asserted).\n  `pff_premium` per-season totals now equal the pre-load backup (2024: 126,827; 2025: 152,430).\n  Safety copy taken before the restore: `data/pff_before_restore_premium_20260922.db`.\n- No other table lost rows in any season (`games`, `pff_grades`, `pff_stats`,\n  `player_seasons` checked per season against the backup).\n\n## Decisions\n- Restored locally only. Did **not** export to Drive tonight: Eric was signing off, and an\n  export overwrites the Windows-written 2024/2025 files.\n\n## Next\n1. Fix `load_snapshot.py` (and maybe `export_snapshot.py`): for `pff_premium`, replace by\n   (season, category), not by season. Or refuse the load when the local DB has a category\n   the snapshot lacks. Add a test with a Mac-only category.\n2. Export 2024 and 2025 from the Mac so Windows gets the four categories.\n3. Until 1 and 2 are done: Windows must not export 2024/2025. The Mac must not load again.\n\n## Files\n- `data/pff.db` (restored rows; not in git)\n- `data/pff_before_restore_premium_20260922.db` (new backup; not in git)\n- `docs/STATUS.md`, this file\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1403,"cache_read_input_tokens":110207,"output_tokens":1117,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":33},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1403,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1117,"cache_read_input_tokens":110207,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1403,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1403},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Gjz42FDRyzn7yPFEJ7LPcH":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project/docs/handoffs/2026-09-22-mac-snapshot-load-restore.md","content":"# 2026-09-22 (Mac, evening): snapshot load, data loss found, rows restored\n\n## What happened\n- Eric ran `scripts/load_snapshot.py` on the Mac at 18:15 to take the Windows export\n  (2023-2026, 22 files, written by BU-1979FJ4 at 22:39 UTC). Backup made by the script:\n  `data/pff_before_load_snapshot_20260922_181535.db`.\n- Verification: `--dry-run` rerun shows all 22 files `same`. 2026 `games`, `pff_grades`,\n  `pff_premium` compared row by row (EXCEPT ALL both ways): 0 differences.\n- **Bug found:** the load deletes each season in the snapshot, then inserts the snapshot's\n  rows. Windows never had the Mac-only `pff_premium` categories, so the Mac lost them:\n\n  | season | category | rows lost |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | 2024 | video_plays | 2,302 |\n  | 2024 | team_play | 2,302 |\n  | 2024 | quarterback_charting | 992 |\n  | 2024 | rushing | 887 |\n  | 2025 | video_plays | 2,215 |\n  | 2025 | team_play | 2,215 |\n  | 2025 | quarterback_charting | 1,014 |\n  | 2025 | rushing | 823 |\n\n- **Restored** the same night: `INSERT INTO pff_premium SELECT * FROM <pre-load backup>`\n  for those 8 (season, category) pairs. The pairs were empty before the insert (asserted).\n  `pff_premium` per-season totals now equal the pre-load backup (2024: 126,827; 2025: 152,430).\n  Safety copy taken before the restore: `data/pff_before_restore_premium_20260922.db`.\n- No other table lost rows in any season (`games`, `pff_grades`, `pff_stats`,\n  `player_seasons` checked per season against the backup).\n\n## Decisions\n- Restored locally only. Did **not** export to Drive tonight: Eric was signing off, and an\n  export overwrites the Windows-written 2024/2025 files.\n\n## Next\n1. Fix `load_snapshot.py` (and maybe `export_snapshot.py`): for `pff_premium`, replace by\n   (season, category), not by season. Or refuse the load when the local DB has a category\n   the snapshot lacks. Add a test with a Mac-only category.\n2. Export 2024 and 2025 from the Mac so Windows gets the four categories.\n3. Until 1 and 2 are done: Windows must not export 2024/2025. The Mac must not load again.\n\n## Files\n- `data/pff.db` (restored rows; not in git)\n- `data/pff_before_restore_premium_20260922.db` (new backup; not in git)\n- `docs/STATUS.md`, this file\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfKLeKAq3cJVm6XpfbnKi","attributionSkill":"closeout","type":"assistant","uuid":"167e7fad-22c8-407d-adea-da377ca97545","timestamp":"2026-09-22T23:23:52.559Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project","sessionId":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","version":"2.1.280","gitBranch":"main"}
