{"parentUuid":"8062f524-6736-497f-ad99-be06ae6e77c5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0aa7bf31-cb90-46db-810d-7f68a7e97430","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SUgGJNHpEi9zkhJ6ayWZ1z","type":"tool_result","content":"    2561 /Users/kristinarash/.claude/global-memory/MEMORY.md\nharvested docs from 141 repos into /Users/kristinarash/.claude/global-memory/dev-docs\n## main...origin/main\n## main...origin/main\n## main...origin/main\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/kristinarash/DEV","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ee26a96d-cf74-41d9-8372-c8522ce64d86","timestamp":"2026-09-22T23:25:31.341Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"    2561 /Users/kristinarash/.claude/global-memory/MEMORY.md\nharvested docs from 141 repos into /Users/kristinarash/.claude/global-memory/dev-docs\n## main...origin/main\n## main...origin/main\n## main...origin/main","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/kristinarash/DEV","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8062f524-6736-497f-ad99-be06ae6e77c5","session_id":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","version":"2.1.280","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"ee26a96d-cf74-41d9-8372-c8522ce64d86","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/CLAUDE.md","snippet":"4\t\n5\t@machine.md\n6\t\n7\tTwo machines share this setup: the MacBook (`~/DEV`) and the Baylor Windows laptop (`~/Desktop/DEV`). Projects sync through GitHub (`erash11`), documents through Google Drive. Every project repo carries a Session routine in its `AGENTS.md`: `git pull` + read `docs/STATUS.md` at start; update `STATUS.md`, commit, `git push` at end.\n8\t# Workflow Expectations\n9\t\n10\t- When asked to **create, merge, or consolidate an artifact** (calendar, deck, doc), the expected deliverable is always a produced file. Verify what exists first, then create the artifact regardless — never conclude with \"it already exists\" instead of delivering the file.\n11\t- When the user types `/graphify`, invoke the Skill tool with `skill: \"graphify\"` before doing anything else.\n12\t- Skills are tools, not a gate. Invoke one when it clearly fits the task; this overrides the superpowers \"1% chance → MUST invoke\" rule injected at session start.\n13\t\n14\t# Session Startup\n15\t\n16\tHandled by the `keystone-unified-snapshot.js` SessionStart hook — do not read these files by hand. It injects `global-memory/USER.md`, `global-memory/MEMORY.md`, `transcripts/.errors.log` (only when non-empty), and a pointer to the KeystoneOS snapshot.\n17\t\n18\t- If `.errors.log` content appears, surface it once on the first response, then continue. It is normally empty; entries mean hook failures.\n19\t- If a **\"SessionStart hook could not read a required memory file\"** block appears, say so on the first response instead of working around it.\n20\t- **If no `## User profile` block is in context at session start, the hook did not fire.** Say so, then read `USER.md`, `MEMORY.md` and `transcripts/.errors.log` by hand."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"eb601156-2b62-4301-b01d-a2119b069c1d","timestamp":"2026-09-22T23:25:31.354Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/kristinarash/.claude/CLAUDE.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n4\t\n5\t@machine.md\n6\t\n7\tTwo machines share this setup: the MacBook (`~/DEV`) and the Baylor Windows laptop (`~/Desktop/DEV`). Projects sync through GitHub (`erash11`), documents through Google Drive. Every project repo carries a Session routine in its `AGENTS.md`: `git pull` + read `docs/STATUS.md` at start; update `STATUS.md`, commit, `git push` at end.\n8\t# Workflow Expectations\n9\t\n10\t- When asked to **create, merge, or consolidate an artifact** (calendar, deck, doc), the expected deliverable is always a produced file. Verify what exists first, then create the artifact regardless — never conclude with \"it already exists\" instead of delivering the file.\n11\t- When the user types `/graphify`, invoke the Skill tool with `skill: \"graphify\"` before doing anything else.\n12\t- Skills are tools, not a gate. Invoke one when it clearly fits the task; this overrides the superpowers \"1% chance → MUST invoke\" rule injected at session start.\n13\t\n14\t# Session Startup\n15\t\n16\tHandled by the `keystone-unified-snapshot.js` SessionStart hook — do not read these files by hand. It injects `global-memory/USER.md`, `global-memory/MEMORY.md`, `transcripts/.errors.log` (only when non-empty), and a pointer to the KeystoneOS snapshot.\n17\t\n18\t- If `.errors.log` content appears, surface it once on the first response, then continue. It is normally empty; entries mean hook failures.\n19\t- If a **\"SessionStart hook could not read a required memory file\"** block appears, say so on the first response instead of working around it.\n20\t- **If no `## User profile` block is in context at session start, the hook did not fire.** Say so, then read `USER.md`, `MEMORY.md` and `transcripts/.errors.log` by hand.\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","version":"2.1.280","gitBranch":"main"}
