{"parentUuid":"50df6b53-bf3b-42f1-b309-d75cf4061210","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fddbbb96-9f74-4dc8-bbbe-b3bcc5cb7f45","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019Sxc6QWYiainkN4wke8fom","type":"tool_result","content":"  Decision (Eric): EPA (PFF current) is the EPA source going forward.\n\n## Next\n1. ~~Fix `load_snapshot.py`~~ **Fixed 2026-09-22** (PR #4): the load merges by primary key\n   and never deletes. The 12,750 Mac-only rows erased by the old load were restored from\n   the pre-load backup. Real dry run on the Mac now reports \"keeps 6,483 / 6,267 local-only\".\n2. **Then export from the Mac** (`python scripts/export_snapshot.py --season 2024 --season 2025`)\n   so Windows gets those rows. Windows: `git pull` before any load.\n3. Pull 2026 weekly with `scripts/pull_season_video_plays.py --season 2026 --refresh`, so\n   MatchupAnalysis opponent profiles can quote EPA (PFF current) instead of CFBD PPA.\n   **Video plays are still Mac-only on this box** - the 09-13 ingests never reached\n   Windows, and `load_snapshot.py` moves them once the Mac exports.\n4. Re-run `--season 2026` weekly during the season; each run adds the graded week.\n## Gotchas\n- A load never deletes, so a row removed upstream lingers locally. Harmless today: the\n  pipeline's own upserts never delete either.\n- The Mac's plain `python3` has no `duckdb`. Use `~/.local/bin/uv run --with-requirements requirements.txt --with pyarrow python ...`.\n- The season feed is about 2.5 GB decoded; stream it (ijson), never `response.json()`.\n- `season_plays.to_frame` needs `dtype=object`, or gappy int columns land as `\"2.0\"`/`\"nan\"`.\n- Bowl-week rows carry week \"BG\"; take season and week from the games list.\n\n---","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f197e44f-bfc2-428c-b037-fe7faf5b22b4","timestamp":"2026-09-22T23:29:07.594Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"  Decision (Eric): EPA (PFF current) is the EPA source going forward.\n\n## Next\n1. ~~Fix `load_snapshot.py`~~ **Fixed 2026-09-22** (PR #4): the load merges by primary key\n   and never deletes. The 12,750 Mac-only rows erased by the old load were restored from\n   the pre-load backup. Real dry run on the Mac now reports \"keeps 6,483 / 6,267 local-only\".\n2. **Then export from the Mac** (`python scripts/export_snapshot.py --season 2024 --season 2025`)\n   so Windows gets those rows. Windows: `git pull` before any load.\n3. Pull 2026 weekly with `scripts/pull_season_video_plays.py --season 2026 --refresh`, so\n   MatchupAnalysis opponent profiles can quote EPA (PFF current) instead of CFBD PPA.\n   **Video plays are still Mac-only on this box** - the 09-13 ingests never reached\n   Windows, and `load_snapshot.py` moves them once the Mac exports.\n4. Re-run `--season 2026` weekly during the season; each run adds the graded week.\n## Gotchas\n- A load never deletes, so a row removed upstream lingers locally. Harmless today: the\n  pipeline's own upserts never delete either.\n- The Mac's plain `python3` has no `duckdb`. Use `~/.local/bin/uv run --with-requirements requirements.txt --with pyarrow python ...`.\n- The season feed is about 2.5 GB decoded; stream it (ijson), never `response.json()`.\n- `season_plays.to_frame` needs `dtype=object`, or gappy int columns land as `\"2.0\"`/`\"nan\"`.\n- Bowl-week rows carry week \"BG\"; take season and week from the games list.\n\n---","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project/AGENTS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":177,"oldLines":8,"newStart":177,"newLines":10,"lines":["   1.33 M rows, is about 6 MB."," - `manifest.json` records rows, bytes, which machine wrote it and when. An export","   merges into it, so exporting one season never erases the record of the others.","-- The load is season-scoped and idempotent: it deletes and reinserts only the seasons","-  the snapshot carries, leaves the rest alone, and backs the DB up first.","+- The load merges by primary key and never deletes: snapshot rows are added or replace","+  the matching local row; rows only this machine has are kept (the dry run says how","+  many). Idempotent, and it backs the DB up first. It used to delete each season first,","+  which erased the Mac's video_plays on 2026-09-22; `tests/test_snapshot.py` guards it."," - `ingest_log` is never exported. It says what **this** machine fetched; copying it","   would make the other machine's history a lie."," - After `dev-sync` pulls the scripts, run `load_snapshot.py` to pull the data. Git"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project/CLAUDE.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":177,"oldLines":8,"newStart":177,"newLines":10,"lines":["   1.33 M rows, is about 6 MB."," - `manifest.json` records rows, bytes, which machine wrote it and when. An export","   merges into it, so exporting one season never erases the record of the others.","-- The load is season-scoped and idempotent: it deletes and reinserts only the seasons","-  the snapshot carries, leaves the rest alone, and backs the DB up first.","+- The load merges by primary key and never deletes: snapshot rows are added or replace","+  the matching local row; rows only this machine has are kept (the dry run says how","+  many). Idempotent, and it backs the DB up first. It used to delete each season first,","+  which erased the Mac's video_plays on 2026-09-22; `tests/test_snapshot.py` guards it."," - `ingest_log` is never exported. It says what **this** machine fetched; copying it","   would make the other machine's history a lie."," - After `dev-sync` pulls the scripts, run `load_snapshot.py` to pull the data. Git"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project/docs/STATUS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":14,"oldLines":7,"newStart":14,"newLines":7,"lines":["   manifest. The whole 612 MB DB is **40 MB** of Parquet; all of 2026 is 6 MB. A full","   snapshot of 2023-2026 is on Drive now, so the Mac can catch up without touching the API."," - **Mac loaded the snapshot 2026-09-22 18:15** and matches it (22 files, all counts equal;","-  2026 checked row by row). Load bug found and repaired the same night: see Next 1.","+  2026 checked row by row). Load bug found, data restored and the script fixed the same night (PR #4)."," "," ## Done"," - Repo brought under git and pushed to erash11 (2026-09-09)."]},{"oldStart":38,"oldLines":14,"newStart":38,"newLines":11,"lines":["   Decision (Eric): EPA (PFF current) is the EPA source going forward."," "," ## Next","-1. **Fix `load_snapshot.py` before anyone loads again.** It deletes a whole season, then","-   inserts only what the snapshot has. On 2026-09-22 the Mac load erased 12,750 Mac-only","-   `pff_premium` rows (2024-2025: `video_plays`, `team_play`, `quarterback_charting`,","-   `rushing`). They were restored from the pre-load backup the same night. Fix idea:","-   replace per (season, category) for `pff_premium`, or refuse when local has a category","-   the snapshot lacks. See `docs/handoffs/2026-09-22-mac-snapshot-load-restore.md`.","+1. ~~Fix `load_snapshot.py`~~ **Fixed 2026-09-22** (PR #4): the load merges by primary key","+   and never deletes. The 12,750 Mac-only rows erased by the old load were restored from","+   the pre-load backup. Real dry run on the Mac now reports \"keeps 6,483 / 6,267 local-only\"."," 2. **Then export from the Mac** (`python scripts/export_snapshot.py --season 2024 --season 2025`)","-   so Windows gets those rows. Until then, **Windows must not export 2024/2025 over them.**","+   so Windows gets those rows. Windows: `git pull` before any load."," 3. Pull 2026 weekly with `scripts/pull_season_video_plays.py --season 2026 --refresh`, so","    MatchupAnalysis opponent profiles can quote EPA (PFF current) instead of CFBD PPA.","    **Video plays are still Mac-only on this box** - the 09-13 ingests never reached"]},{"oldStart":57,"oldLines":8,"newStart":54,"newLines":8,"lines":[" - None waiting on Eric."," "," ## Gotchas","-- `load_snapshot.py` is season-scoped: any local row the snapshot lacks for that season is","-  deleted. Run `--dry-run` AND compare `pff_premium` categories before a real load.","+- A load never deletes, so a row removed upstream lingers locally. Harmless today: the","+  pipeline's own upserts never delete either."," - The Mac's plain `python3` has no `duckdb`. Use `~/.local/bin/uv run --with-requirements requirements.txt --with pyarrow python ...`."," - The season feed is about 2.5 GB decoded; stream it (ijson), never `response.json()`."," - `season_plays.to_frame` needs `dtype=object`, or gappy int columns land as `\"2.0\"`/`\"nan\"`."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project/AGENTS.md","/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project/CLAUDE.md","/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project/docs/STATUS.md"]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"50df6b53-bf3b-42f1-b309-d75cf4061210","session_id":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project","sessionId":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","version":"2.1.280","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"f197e44f-bfc2-428c-b037-fe7faf5b22b4","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project/CLAUDE.md","snippet":"172\twritten once, never mutated, so a half-synced file cannot corrupt anything.\n173\t\n174\t- Root: `$PFF_SNAPSHOT_DIR`, else `.../00_Primary_Storage_Drive/pff-snapshots`.\n175\t- One file per table per season (`pff_grades/season=2026.parquet`), so a single season\n176\t  moves without dragging six million rows behind it. It is small: all of 2026,\n177\t  1.33 M rows, is about 6 MB.\n178\t- `manifest.json` records rows, bytes, which machine wrote it and when. An export\n179\t  merges into it, so exporting one season never erases the record of the others.\n180\t- The load merges by primary key and never deletes: snapshot rows are added or replace\n181\t  the matching local row; rows only this machine has are kept (the dry run says how\n182\t  many). Idempotent, and it backs the DB up first. It used to delete each season first,\n183\t  which erased the Mac's video_plays on 2026-09-22; `tests/test_snapshot.py` guards it.\n184\t- `ingest_log` is never exported. It says what **this** machine fetched; copying it\n185\t  would make the other machine's history a lie.\n186\t- After `dev-sync` pulls the scripts, run `load_snapshot.py` to pull the data. Git\n187\t  carries the code, Drive carries the rows.\n188\t\n189\t## Testing\n190\t\n191\t```"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d3640ec1-5fcb-4d42-aa1c-889e2b284c18","timestamp":"2026-09-22T23:29:07.620Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project/CLAUDE.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n172\twritten once, never mutated, so a half-synced file cannot corrupt anything.\n173\t\n174\t- Root: `$PFF_SNAPSHOT_DIR`, else `.../00_Primary_Storage_Drive/pff-snapshots`.\n175\t- One file per table per season (`pff_grades/season=2026.parquet`), so a single season\n176\t  moves without dragging six million rows behind it. It is small: all of 2026,\n177\t  1.33 M rows, is about 6 MB.\n178\t- `manifest.json` records rows, bytes, which machine wrote it and when. An export\n179\t  merges into it, so exporting one season never erases the record of the others.\n180\t- The load merges by primary key and never deletes: snapshot rows are added or replace\n181\t  the matching local row; rows only this machine has are kept (the dry run says how\n182\t  many). Idempotent, and it backs the DB up first. It used to delete each season first,\n183\t  which erased the Mac's video_plays on 2026-09-22; `tests/test_snapshot.py` guards it.\n184\t- `ingest_log` is never exported. It says what **this** machine fetched; copying it\n185\t  would make the other machine's history a lie.\n186\t- After `dev-sync` pulls the scripts, run `load_snapshot.py` to pull the data. Git\n187\t  carries the code, Drive carries the rows.\n188\t\n189\t## Testing\n190\t\n191\t```\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project","sessionId":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","version":"2.1.280","gitBranch":"main"}
