{"parentUuid":"fed8eb10-4f34-45df-9e97-19831cf49970","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfKM63Hq2tchvxUnbP544","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The load fix is done and merged. The load no longer deletes rows.\n\n**What changed**\n- **Before:** the load deleted each season, then copied in the snapshot. Any row that was only on this machine was lost.\n- **Now:** the load only adds new rows and updates matching rows. Rows that only this machine has stay.\n- **Dry run:** it now shows 2 numbers for each file: how many rows the load will add, and how many rows it will keep that only this machine has.\n- It still checks each file's row count against `manifest.json`.\n\n**Did it work? Yes.**\n- I added a new test for this exact bug. It failed on the old code and passes on the new code. All 50 tests pass.\n- On your real Mac database, the dry run now says it keeps 6,483 rows (2024) and 6,267 rows (2025). That is the 12,750 rows the old load deleted. It adds 0 rows, because the Mac already has everything in the snapshot.\n- PR #4 is merged into `main`: https://github.com/erash11/PFF_Data_Project/pull/4\n- I also updated `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `docs/STATUS.md` and MEMORY.md. All are pushed.\n\n**What you do next:** export from the Mac, so Windows gets the 12,750 rows:\n```\ncd ~/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project\n~/.local/bin/uv run --with-requirements requirements.txt --with pyarrow python scripts/export_snapshot.py --season 2024 --season 2025\n```\nThen on Windows:\n1. Run `git pull`, so Windows has the fix.\n2. Run `python scripts/load_snapshot.py --dry-run`.\n3. Run `python scripts/load_snapshot.py`.\n\nDo you want me to run the export now?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":556,"cache_read_input_tokens":137281,"output_tokens":596,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":556,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":596,"cache_read_input_tokens":137281,"cache_creation_input_tokens":556,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":556},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfKM62m5HXbjBPerTFnKy","type":"assistant","uuid":"74a7d30a-48f4-4a28-a458-2ddd41aea075","timestamp":"2026-09-22T23:29:36.942Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"74f6814f-8ccf-42bc-aee0-c087dea07887","version":"2.1.280","gitBranch":"main"}
