{"parentUuid":"bba82c6d-4529-450e-98ff-435b6a033584","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfKMVXJTRpu1tySzPxYjs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The export is done, and the data on Drive now matches the Mac.\n\n**What I did**\n- I exported 2024 and 2025 from the Mac to Drive. That wrote 12 files, plus 2 whole tables: `teams` and `players`.\n- The Drive snapshot now has 6,693,237 rows. Before it had 6,680,487, so it gained 12,750 rows. That is exactly the number of rows that were only on the Mac.\n- I checked with a dry run on the Mac. It adds 0 rows and keeps 0 local-only rows. That means Drive and the Mac have the same data.\n- I updated STATUS.md and MEMORY.md and pushed both.\n\n**What you do next, on Windows:**\n```\ngit pull\npython scripts/load_snapshot.py --dry-run\npython scripts/load_snapshot.py\n```\nDo step 1 first. Without `git pull`, Windows still runs the old load, which deletes rows. In the dry run, look for \"adds 12,750\" in total on the 2024 and 2025 `pff_premium` lines.\n\nEverything is pushed. You are clear to sign off."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":879,"cache_read_input_tokens":139747,"output_tokens":366,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":879,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":366,"cache_read_input_tokens":139747,"cache_creation_input_tokens":879,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":879},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfKMVWfzdCqmzXbXek7sX","type":"assistant","uuid":"985b2254-3ac2-4735-828